{
  "title": "22: al-Hajj الحج",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اتَّقُوْا رَبَّكُمْ‌ۚ اِنَّ زَلْزَلَةَ السَّاعَةِ شَىْءٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO TAQOO TAQUL INNAL ZALZALATA AS-SAAA’ATE SHAY-UN A’ZEEM.\nO mankind! fear your Lord! for the convulsion of the Hour (of Judgment) will be a thing terrible! \nيَوْمَ تَرَوْنَهَا تَذْهَلُ كُلُّ مُرْضِعَةٍ عَمَّاۤ اَرْضَعَتْ وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذَاتِ حَمْلٍ حَمْلَهَا وَتَرَى النَّاسَ سُكٰرٰى وَمَا هُمْ بِسُكٰرٰى وَلٰكِنَّ عَذَابَ اللّٰهِ شَدِيْدٌ‏(2)\nYAWMA TARAWNAHAA TAZHALU KULLO MURZEA’ATIN A’MMAA AARZAA’AT WA TAZAA-O’ KULLO ZAATIL HAMLIN HAMLAHAA WA TARAL NAASA SUKAARAA WA MAA HUM BESUKAARAA LAAKINNAL A’ZAABAL LAAHE SHADEEDUN.\nThe Day ye shall see it, every mother giving suck shall forget her suckling-babe, and every pregnant female shall drop her load (unformed): thou shalt see mankind as in a drunken riot, yet not drunk: but dreadful will be the Wrath of Allah. \nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يُّجَادِلُ فِى اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ وَّيَتَّبِعُ كُلَّ شَيْطٰنٍ مَّرِيْدٍ ۙ‏(3)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN YYUJAADELU FIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN WWAYATTABEU’U KULLA SHAYTAANIR MMAREEDIN.\nAnd yet among men there are such as dispute about Allah, without knowledge, and follow every evil one obstinate in rebellion! \nكُتِبَ عَلَيْهِ اَنَّهٗ مَنْ تَوَلَّاهُ فَاَنَّهٗ يُضِلُّهٗ وَيَهْدِيْهِ اِلٰى عَذَابِ السَّعِيْرِ‏(4)\nKOTEBA A’LAYHE ANNAHU MAN TAWALLAAHU FA ANNAHU YUZELLUH WAYAHDEEHE ELAA A’ZAABIN SA-E’ER.\nAbout the (Evil One) it is decreed that whoever turns to him for friendship, him will he lead astray, and he will guide him to the Penalty of the Fire. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فِىْ رَيْبٍ مِّنَ الْبَعْثِ فَاِنَّا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ عَلَقَةٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ مُّضْغَةٍ مُّخَلَّقَةٍ وَّغَيْرِ مُخَلَّقَةٍ لِّنُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ‌ ؕ وَنُقِرُّ فِى الْاَرْحَامِ مَا نَشَآءُ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى ثُمَّ نُخْرِجُكُمْ طِفْلًا ثُمَّ لِتَبْلُغُوْۤا اَشُدَّكُمْ ‌ۚ وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّتَوَفّٰى وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّرَدُّ اِلٰٓى اَرْذَلِ الْعُمُرِ لِكَيْلَا يَعْلَمَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ عِلْمٍ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَتَرَى الْاَرْضَ هَامِدَةً فَاِذَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْهَا الْمَآءَ اهْتَزَّتْ وَرَبَتْ وَاَنْۢبَتَتْ مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍۢ بَهِيْجٍ‏(5)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO IN KUNTUM FEE RAIBIM MENAL BA’SE WA FAINNAA KHALAQNAAKUM MIN TORAABIN SUMMA MIN NUTFATIN SUMMA MIN A’ALAQATIN SUMMA MIN MMUZGHATIN MMUKHALLAQATIN WWAGHAYRE MUKHALLAQATIN LLENUBAYNA LAKUM WANUQERRU FIL AL-AARHAAME MAA NASHAAA-O ELAA ELAA AJALIM SUMMA NUKHREJUKUM TEFLAN SUMMA LETABLUGHOOA AASHUDDAKUM WA MINKUM MAN YYUTAWAFFAA WA MINKUM MAN YYURADDU ELAA AARZALE AL-U’UMURE LE-KAYLAA YAA’LAMA MIN BA’DE I’LMIN SHAY-ANW WA TARAL ARZA HAAMEDATAN FA-EZAA ANZALNAA A’LAYHAA MAAA-AH TAZZAT WARABAT WA AMBATAT MIN KULLE ZAWJIN BAHEEJIN.\nO mankind! if ye have a doubt about the Resurrection, (consider) that We created you out of dust, then out of sperm, then out of a leech-like clot, then out of a morsel of flesh, partly formed and partly unformed, in order that We may manifest (our power) to you; and We cause whom We will to rest in the wombs for an appointed term, then do We bring you out as babes, then (foster you) that ye may reach your age of full strength; and some of you are called to die, and some are sent back to the feeblest old age, so that they know nothing after having known (much), and (further), thou seest the earth barren and lifeless, but when We pour down rain on it, it is stirred (to life), it swells, and it puts forth every kind of beautiful growth (in pairs). \nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْحَقُّ وَاَنَّهٗ يُحْىِ الْمَوْتٰى وَاَنَّهٗ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ ۙ‏(6)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA HOWA HAQQO WA ANNAHU LAAHUL MAWTAA WA ANNAHU A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nThis is so, because Allah is the Reality: it is He Who gives life to the dead, and it is He Who has power over all things. \nوَّاَنَّ السَّاعَةَ اٰتِيَةٌ لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا ۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَبْعَثُ مَنْ فِى الْقُبُوْرِ‏(7)\nWA ANNAL SAA-A’TA AAATEETUN LAA RAYBA FEEHAA WA ANNAL LAAHA YABA’ASU MAN FIL QOBOORE.\nAnd verily the Hour will come: there can be no doubt about it, or about (the fact) that Allah will raise up all who are in the graves. \nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يُّجَادِلُ فِى اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ وَّلَا هُدًى وَلَا كِتٰبٍ مُّنِيْرٍ ۙ‏(8)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN YYUJAADELU FIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN WA LAA HODAM WA LAA KETAABIM MMUNEERIN.\nYet there is among men such a one as disputes about Allah, without Knowledge, without Guidance, and without a Book of Enlightenment, \nثَانِىَ عِطْفِهٖ لِيُضِلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ‌ؕ لَهٗ فِى الدُّنْيَا خِزْىٌ‌ وَّنُذِيْقُهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عَذَابَ الْحَرِيْقِ‏(9)\nSAANEAAA E’ETFEH LEEZELLA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE LAHU FIL DUNYAA KHIZYUN WWANUZEEQUH YAWMA QEYAAMATE A’ZAABAL AL-HAREEQE.\n(Disdainfully) bending his side, in order to lead (men) astray from the Path of Allah: for him there is disgrace in this life, and on the Day of Judgment We shall make him taste the Penalty of burning (Fire). \nذٰ لِكَ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ يَدٰكَ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَيْسَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِ‏(10)\nZAA LEKA BEMAA QADDAMAT YADAAKA WA ANNAL LAAHA LAYSA BEZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\n(It will be said): “This is because of the deeds which thy hands sent forth, for verily Allah is not unjust to His servants. \nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّعْبُدُ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى حَرْفٍ‌ ‌ۚ فَاِنْ اَصَابَهٗ خَيْرٌ اۨطْمَاَنَّ بِهٖ‌ ۚ وَاِنْ اَصَابَتْهُ فِتْنَةُ اۨنقَلَبَ عَلٰى وَجْهِهٖ‌ۚ خَسِرَ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةَ ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْخُسْرَانُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(11)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN YYAA’BUDU LAAHA A’LAA HARFIN FA-IN AASAABAH KHAYRUL ATMAANNA BEHI WA AASAABATHU FETNATU ANQALABA A’LAA WAJHEHI KHASERA DUNYAA WA AAKHERATA ZAA LEKA HOWA AL-KHUSRAANU MOBEEN.\nThere are among men some who serve Allah, as it were, on the verge: if good befalls them, they are, therewith, well content; but if a trial comes to them, they turn on their faces: they lose both this world and the Hereafter: that is loss for all to see! \nيَدْعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَضُرُّهٗ وَمَا لَا يَنْفَعُهٗ ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الضَّلٰلُ الْبَعِيْدُ‌ ۚ‏(12)\nYAD-O’O MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YAZURRUH WA MAA LAA YANFAU’UH ZAA LEKA HOWA AZ-ZALAALU AL-BAE’EEDU.\nThey call on such deities, besides Allah, as can neither hurt nor profit them: that is straying far indeed (from the Way)! \nيَدْعُوْا لَمَنْ ضَرُّهٗۤ اَقْرَبُ مِنْ نَّفْعِهٖ‌ؕ لَبِئْسَ الْمَوْلٰى وَلَبِئْسَ الْعَشِيْرُ‏(13)\nYAD-O’O LAMAN ZARRUH AQRABO MIN NNAFE’EH LABESA AL-MAWLAA WA LABESA AL-A’ASHEERU.\n(Perhaps) they call on one whose hurt is nearer than his profit: evil, indeed, is the patron, and evil the companion (or help)! \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُدْخِلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يُرِيْدُ‏(14)\nINNAL LAAHA YUDKHELU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO INNAL LAAHA YAF-A’LO MAA YOREEDO.\nVerily Allah will admit those who believe and work righteous deeds, to Gardens, beneath which rivers flow: for Allah carries out all that He plans. \nمَنْ كَانَ يَظُنُّ اَنْ لَّنْ يَّنْصُرَهُ اللّٰهُ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ فَلْيَمْدُدْ بِسَبَبٍ اِلَى السَّمَآءِ ثُمَّ لْيَقْطَعْ فَلْيَنْظُرْ هَلْ يُذْهِبَنَّ كَيْدُهٗ مَا يَغِيْظُ‏(15)\nMAN KAANA YAZUNNO AN LAN-Y YYANSURAHU LAAHO FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH FALYAMDUD BESABABIN ELAL SAMAAA-E SUMMA LYAQTAA’ FALYANZUR HAL YUZHEBANNA KAYDUH MAA YAGHEEZU.\nIf any think that Allah will not help him (His Messenger) in this world and the Hereafter, let him stretch out a rope to the ceiling and cut (himself) off: then let him see whether his plan will remove that which enrages (him)! \nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍۙ وَّاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يُّرِيْدُ‏(16)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAAHO AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT WA ANNAL LAAHA YAHDEE MAN YYUREEDU.\nThus have We sent down Clear Signs; and verily Allah doth guide whom He will! \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَالَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا وَالصّٰبِئِيْنَ وَالنَّصٰرٰى وَالْمَجُوْسَ وَالَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْۤا ‌ۖ  اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(17)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAL LAZEENA HAADOO WAS SAABE-EENA WAN NASAARAA WAL MAJOOSA WAL LAZEENA ASHRAKOO INNAL LAAHA YAFSELU BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WA.\nThose who believe (in the Qur'an), those who follow the Jewish (scriptures), and the Sabians, Christians, Magians, and Polytheists, Allah will judge between them on the Day of Judgment: for Allah is witness of all things. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَسْجُدُ لَهٗ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَالشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ وَالنُّجُوْمُ وَ الْجِبَالُ وَالشَّجَرُ وَالدَّوَآبُّ وَكَثِيْرٌ مِّنَ النَّاسِ‌ ؕ وَكَثِيْرٌ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِ الْعَذَابُ‌ؕ وَمَنْ يُّهِنِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ مُّكْرِمٍ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يَشَآءُ ۩  ؕ‏(18)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA YASJUDU LAHU MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAN FIL ARZE WASH-SHAMSO WAL-QAMARO WA NOJOOMUN WA JEBAALO WASH-SHAJARO WAALDDAWAABBU WA KASEERUM MENAL NAASE WA KASEERUM HAQQA A’LAYHE A’ZAAB WA MAN YYUHENE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN MMUKREMIN INNAL LAAHA YAF-A’LO MAA YASHAAA.\nSeest thou not that to Allah bow down in worship all things that are in the heavens and on earth, the sun, the moon, the stars; the hills, the trees, the animals; and a great number among mankind? But a great number are (also) such as are fit for Punishment: and such as Allah shall disgrace, None can raise to honour: for Allah carries out all that He wills. [۩] \nهٰذٰنِ خَصْمٰنِ اخْتَصَمُوْا فِىْ رَبِّهِمْ‌ فَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا قُطِّعَتْ لَهُمْ ثِيَابٌ مِّنْ نَّارٍ ؕ يُصَبُّ مِنْ فَوْقِ رُءُوْسِهِمُ الْحَمِيْمُ‌ۚ‏(19)\nHAAZAANE KHASMAANE AKHTASAMOOA FEE RABBEHIM FAL LAZEENA KAFAROO QUTTEA’AT LAHUM SEEABUN MIN NAAR YUSABBU MIN FAWQE RUOOSEHEMU AL-HAMEEMU.\nThese two antagonists dispute with each other about their Lord: But those who deny (their Lord), for them will be cut out a garment of Fire: over their heads will be poured out boiling water. \nيُصْهَرُ بِهٖ مَا فِىْ بُطُوْنِهِمْ وَالْجُلُوْدُؕ‏(20)\nYUSHARU BEHI MAA FEE BOTOONEHIM WAL JULOODU.\nWith it will be scalded what is within their bodies, as well as (their) skins. \nوَلَهُمْ مَّقَامِعُ مِنْ حَدِيْدٍ‏(21)\nWA LAHUM MMAQAAMEU’U MIN HADEEDIN.\nIn addition there will be maces of iron (to punish) them. \nكُلَّمَاۤ اَرَادُوْۤا اَنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَا مِنْ غَمٍّ اُعِيْدُوْا فِيْهَا وَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْحَرِيْقِ‏(22)\nKULLAMAA AARAADOOA AN YAKHROJOO MINHAA MIN GHAMMIN AUE’EEDOOA FEEHAA WA ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL AL-HAREEQE.\nEvery time they wish to get away therefrom, from anguish, they will be forced back therein, and (it will be said), “Taste ye the Penalty of Burning!” \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُدْخِلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ يُحَلَّوْنَ فِيْهَا مِنْ اَسَاوِرَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ وَّلُؤْلُؤًا ‌ؕ وَلِبَاسُهُمْ فِيْهَا حَرِيْرٌ‏(23)\nINNAL LAAHA YUDKHELU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO YUHALLAWNA FEEHAA MIN ASAAWERA MIN ZAHABIN WWALULUAN WALEBAASUHUM FEEHAA HAREERUN.\nAllah will admit those who believe and work righteous deeds, to Gardens beneath which rivers flow: they shall be adorned therein with bracelets of gold and pearls; and their garments there will be of silk. \nوَهُدُوْۤا اِلَى الطَّيِّبِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ‌ ۖۚ وَهُدُوْۤا اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْحَمِيْدِ‏(24)\nWAHUDOOA ELAL AT-TAYBE MENAL AL-QAWLE WAHUDOOA ELAA SERAATE HAMEEDIL.\nFor they have been guided (in this life) to the purest of speeches; they have been guided to the Path of Him Who is Worthy of (all) Praise. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَيَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ الَّذِىْ جَعَلْنٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ سَوَآءَ اۨلْعَاكِفُ فِيْهِ وَالْبَادِ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّرِدْ فِيْهِ بِاِلْحَادٍۢ بِظُلْمٍ نُّذِقْهُ مِنْ عَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(25)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WAL MASJEDIL HARAAME LAZEE LAW LIN-NAASE SAWAAA-AS AL-A’AAKEFU FEEHE WAL BAADE WA MAN YYURED FEEHE BEAELHAADIN BEZULMIN NNUZEQHU MIN A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nAs to those who have rejected (Allah), and would keep back (men) from the Way of Allah, and from the Sacred Mosque, which We have made (open) to (all) men - equal is the dweller there and the visitor from the country - and any whose purpose therein is profanity or wrong-doing - them will We cause to taste of a most Grievous Penalty. \nوَاِذْ بَوَّاْنَا لِاِبْرٰهِيْمَ مَكَانَ الْبَيْتِ اَنْ لَّا تُشْرِكْ بِىْ شَيْئًا وَّطَهِّرْ بَيْتِىَ لِلطَّآئِفِيْنَ وَالْقَآئِمِيْنَ وَ الرُّكَّعِ السُّجُوْدِ‏(26)\nWA IZ BAWANAA LE-IBRAAHEEMA MAKAANA BAYTE AN LAA TUSHREK BEE SHAY-ANW WWATAHHER BAYTEYA LIT-TAAA-EFEENA WAL QAAEMEENA WA AR-RUKKAE’E SOJOOD.\nBehold! We gave the site, to Abraham, of the (Sacred) House, (saying): “Associate not anything (in worship) with Me; and sanctify My House for those who compass it round, or stand up, or bow, or prostrate themselves (therein in prayer). \nوَاَذِّنْ فِى النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ يَاْتُوْكَ رِجَالًا وَّعَلٰى كُلِّ ضَامِرٍ يَّاْتِيْنَ مِنْ كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيْقٍ ۙ‏(27)\nWAAZZEN FIL NAASE BE-HAJJE WA YAATOOKA REJAALAN WWAA’ALAA KULLE ZAAMERIN YAKHRUJNA MIN KULLE FAJJIN A’AMEEQIN.\n“And proclaim the Pilgrimage among men: they will come to thee on foot and (mounted) on every kind of camel, lean on account of journeys through deep and distant mountain highways; \nلِّيَشْهَدُوْا مَنَافِعَ لَهُمْ وَيَذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ فِىْۤ اَ يَّامٍ مَّعْلُوْمٰتٍ عَلٰى مَا رَزَقَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَهِيْمَةِ الْاَنْعَامِ‌‌ ۚ فَكُلُوْا مِنْهَا وَاَطْعِمُوا الْبَآئِسَ الْفَقِيْرَ‏(28)\nLLEESHHADOOA MANAAFEA’A LAHUM WAYAZKUROOA KORISMA LAAHE FEE AYYAAMIN MMAA’LOOMAATIN A’LAA MAA RAZAQAHUM MIN BAHEEMATE AL-AANA’AAME FA-KOLOO MINHAA WAATE’EMOOA AL-BAAESA AL-FAQEERA.\n“That they may witness the benefits (provided) for them, and celebrate the name of Allah, through the Days appointed, over the cattle which He has provided for them (for sacrifice): then eat ye thereof and feed the distressed ones in want. \nثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوْا تَفَثَهُمْ وَلْيُوْفُوْا نُذُوْرَهُمْ وَلْيَطَّوَّفُوْا بِالْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيْقِ‏(29)\nSUMMA LYAQZOOA TAFASAHUM WALYOOFOOA NUZOORAHUM WALYATTAWFOOA BE-BAYTE AL-A’ATEEQE.\n“Then let them complete the rites prescribed for them, perform their vows, and (again) circumambulate the Ancient House.” \nذٰلِكَ وَمَنْ يُّعَظِّمْ حُرُمٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ‌ؕ وَاُحِلَّتْ لَكُمُ الْاَنْعَامُ اِلَّا مَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ‌ فَاجْتَنِبُوا الرِّجْسَ مِنَ الْاَوْثَانِ وَاجْتَنِبُوْا قَوْلَ الزُّوْرِۙ‏(30)\nZAALEKA WA MAN YYUA’AZZEM HURUMAATE LAAHE FAHOWA KHAYRUL LAHU I’NDAL RABBEH WAAHELLAT LAKOMUL AL-AANA’AAMU ILLAA MAA YUTLAA A’LAYKUM FAAJTANEBOOA A’NKOMUR MENAL AL-AAWSAANE WAAJTANEBOOA QAWLA AZ-ZOORE.\nSuch (is the Pilgrimage): whoever honours the sacred rites of Allah, for him it is good in the Sight of his Lord. Lawful to you (for food in Pilgrimage) are cattle, except those mentioned to you (as exception): but shun the abomination of idols, and shun the word that is false, \nحُنَفَآءَ لِلّٰهِ غَيْرَ مُشْرِكِيْنَ بِهٖ‌ؕ وَمَنْ يُّشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ فَكَاَنَّمَا خَرَّ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ فَتَخْطَفُهُ الطَّيْرُ اَوْ تَهْوِىْ بِهِ الرِّيْحُ فِىْ مَكَانٍ سَحِيْقٍ‏(31)\nHONAFAAA-A LILLAAHE GHAYRA MUSHREKEENA BEH WA MAN YYUSHREK BIL-LAAHE FAKAANNAMAA KHARRA MENAL SAMAAA-E FATAKHTAFUHU AT-TAYRU AW TAHWEAA BEHIL AR-REEHU FEE MAKAANIN SAHEEQIN.\nBeing true in faith to Allah, and never assigning partners to Him: if anyone assigns partners to Allah, is as if he had fallen from heaven and been snatched up by birds, or the wind had swooped (like a bird on its prey) and thrown him into a far-distant place. \nذٰلِكَ وَمَنْ يُّعَظِّمْ شَعَآئِرَ اللّٰهِ فَاِنَّهَا مِنْ تَقْوَى الْقُلُوْبِ‏(32)\nZAALEKA WA MAN YYUA’AZZEM SHAA’AAERA LAAHE FA INNAHAA MIN TAQWAA AL-QULOOBE.\nSuch (is his state): and whoever holds in honour the symbols of Allah, (in the sacrifice of animals), such (honour) should come truly from piety of heart. \nلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى ثُمَّ مَحِلُّهَاۤ اِلَى الْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيْقِ‏(33)\nLAKUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ ELAA ELAA AJALIM SUMMA MAHELLUHAA ELAL BAYTE AL-A’ATEEQE.\nIn them ye have benefits for a term appointed: in the end their place of sacrifice is near the Ancient House. \nوَلِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ جَعَلْنَا مَنْسَكًا لِّيَذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ عَلٰى مَا رَزَقَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَهِيْمَةِ الْاَنْعَامِ ؕ فَاِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ فَلَهٗۤ اَسْلِمُوْا‌ ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُخْبِتِيْنَ ۙ‏(34)\nWA LEKULLIM UMMATIN JA-A’LNAA MANSAKAN LLEEZKUROOA KORISMA LAAHE A’LAA MAA RAZAQAHUM MIN BAHEEMATE AL-AANA’AAME FA ELAAHOKUM ELAAHUN WAAHED FALAHU AASLEMOOA WA BASH-SHERIL AL-MUKHBETEENA.\nTo every people did We appoint rites (of sacrifice), that they might celebrate the name of Allah over the sustenance He gave them from animals (fit for food). But your god is One God: submit then your wills to Him (in Islam): and give thou the good news to those who humble themselves, \nالَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِرَ اللّٰهُ وَجِلَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَالصّٰبِرِيْنَ عَلٰى مَاۤ اَصَابَهُمْ وَالْمُقِيْمِى الصَّلٰوةِ ۙ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‏(35)\nLAZEENA EZAA ZUKERA LAAHO WAJELAT QULOOBUHUM WAS SAABEREENA A’LAA MAA AASAABAHUM WAL MUQEEMEAA AS-SALAAWTE WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOONA.\nTo those whose hearts when Allah is mentioned, are filled with fear, who show patient perseverance over their afflictions, keep up regular prayer, and spend (in charity) out of what We have bestowed upon them. \nوَالْبُدْنَ جَعَلْنٰهَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ شَعَآئِرِ اللّٰهِ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا خَيْرٌ‌ ‌ۖ  فَاذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهَا صَوَآفَّ‌ ۚ فَاِذَا وَجَبَتْ جُنُوْبُهَا فَكُلُوْا مِنْهَا وَاَطْعِمُوا الْقَانِعَ وَالْمُعْتَرَّ ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ سَخَّرْنٰهَا لَكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(36)\nWAL BUDNA JA-A’LNAAHAA LAKUM MIN SHA-A’AA-ERIL LAAHE LAKUM FEEHAA KHAYRUL FAZKORUL KORISMA LAAHE A’LAYHAA SAWAAFFA FA-EZAA WAJABAT JUNOOBUHAA FA-KOLOO MINHAA WAATE’EMOOA AL-QAANEA’A WAL MUA’TARRA KAZAALEKA SAKKHARNAAHAA LAKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nThe sacrificial camels we have made for you as among the symbols from Allah: in them is (much) good for you: then pronounce the name of Allah over them as they line up (for sacrifice): when they are down on their sides (after slaughter), eat ye thereof, and feed such as (beg not but) live in contentment, and such as beg with due humility: thus have We made animals subject to you, that ye may be grateful. \nلَنْ يَّنَالَ اللّٰهَ لُحُوْمُهَا وَلَا دِمَآؤُهَا وَلٰكِنْ يَّنَالُهُ التَّقْوٰى مِنْكُمْ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ سَخَّرَهَا لَكُمْ لِتُكَبِّرُوا اللّٰهَ عَلٰى مَا هَدٰٮكُمْ‌ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(37)\nLAN YYANAALA LAAHA LUHOOMUHAA WA LAA DEMAAUHAA WA LAAKIL YYANAALUHU TAQWAA MENKUM KAZAALEKA SAKKHARAHAA LAKUM LETUKABBEROOA LAAHA A’LAA MAA HADAAKUM WA BASH-SHERIL MOHSENEEN.\nIt is not their meat nor their blood, that reaches Allah: it is your piety that reaches Him: He has thus made them subject to you, that ye may glorify Allah for His Guidance to you and proclaim the good news to all who do right. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُدٰفِعُ عَنِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْٓا‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ خَوَّانٍ كَفُوْرٍ‏(38)\nINNAL LAAHA YUDAAFEU’U A’NIL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL KULLA KHAWANIN KAFOORIN.\nVerily Allah will defend (from ill) those who believe: verily, Allah loveth not any that is a traitor to faith, or show ingratitude. \nاُذِنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ يُقٰتَلُوْنَ بِاَنَّهُمْ ظُلِمُوْا‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى نَصْرِهِمْ لَقَدِيْرُ ۙ‏(39)\nAUZENA LILLAZEENA YUQAATALOONA BE-ANNAHUM ZULEMOOA WA INNA LAAHA A’LAA NASREHEM LAQADEERU.\nTo those against whom war is made, permission is given (to fight), because they are wronged;- and verily, Allah is most powerful for their aid;- \nاۨلَّذِيْنَ اُخْرِجُوْا مِنْ دِيَارِهِمْ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّقُوْلُوْا رَبُّنَا اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ وَلَوْلَا دَ فْعُ اللّٰهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لَّهُدِّمَتْ صَوَامِعُ وَبِيَعٌ وَّصَلَوٰتٌ وَّمَسٰجِدُ يُذْكَرُ فِيْهَا اسْمُ اللّٰهِ كَثِيْرًا‌ ؕ وَلَيَنْصُرَنَّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّنْصُرُهٗ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَقَوِىٌّ عَزِيْزٌ‏(40)\nLAZEENA UKHREJOO MIN DEYAAREHIM BEGHAYRIL HAQQIN ILLAA AN YAQOOLOO RABBONAA LAAHO WA LAWLAA DA FU’U LAAHE NAASA BA’ZAHUM BE-BA’Z LLAHUDDEMAT SAWAAMEU’U WABEEA’UN WWASALAWTUN WWAMASAAJEDU YUZKARU FEEHAA RABBEKA LAAHE KASEERAA WALAYANSURANNA LAAHO MAN YYANSURUH INNAL LAAHA LAQAWIYYUN A’ZEEZUN.\n(They are) those who have been expelled from their homes in defiance of right, (for no cause) except that they say, “our Lord is Allah”. Did not Allah check one set of people by means of another, there would surely have been pulled down monasteries, churches, synagogues, and mosques, in which the name of Allah is commemorated in abundant measure. Allah will certainly aid those who aid his (cause);- for verily Allah is full of Strength, Exalted in Might, (able to enforce His Will). \nاَ لَّذِيْنَ اِنْ مَّكَّنّٰهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاَمَرُوْا بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَنَهَوْا عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ‌ ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ عَاقِبَةُ الْاُمُوْرِ‏(41)\nLAZEENA IN MMAKKANNAAHUM FIL ARZE AAQAAMOOA SALAATA WA AATAWUZ ZAKAATA WAAMAROOA BIL-MA’ROOF WANAHAWA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE LILLAAHE A’AQEBATUL AL-AUMOORE.\n(They are) those who, if We establish them in the land, establish regular prayer and give regular charity, enjoin the right and forbid wrong: with Allah rests the end (and decision) of (all) affairs. \nوَاِنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْكَ فَقَدْ كَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٌ وَّثَمُوْدُ ۙ‏(42)\nWA YYUKAZZEBOOKA FAQAD KAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN WWAA’AADUN WWASAMOODU.\nIf they treat thy (mission) as false, so did the peoples before them (with their prophets), the People of Noah, and 'Ad and Thamud; \nوَقَوْمُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَقَوْمُ لُوْطٍ ۙ‏(43)\nWA QAWMO IBRAAHEEMA WA QAWMO LOOTIM.\nThose of Abraham and Lut; \nوَّاَصْحٰبُ مَدْيَنَ‌ۚ وَكُذِّبَ مُوْسٰى فَاَمْلَيْتُ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ ثُمَّ اَخَذْتُهُمْ‌ۚ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ نَكِيْرِ‏(44)\nWWAASHAABU MADYANA WAKUZZEBA MOOSAA FAAMLAYTU LIL KAAFEREENA SUMMA AAKHAZTUHUM FA-KAYFA KAANA NAKEER.\nAnd the Companions of the Madyan People; and Moses was rejected (in the same way). But I granted respite to the Unbelievers, and (only) after that did I punish them: but how (terrible) was my rejection (of them)! \nفَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اَهْلَكْنٰهَا وَهِىَ ظَالِمَةٌ فَهِىَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلٰى عُرُوْشِهَا وَبِئْرٍ مُّعَطَّلَةٍ وَّقَصْرٍ مَّشِيْدٍ‏(45)\nFAKAAYYEN MIN QARYATINW AAHLAKNAAHAA WA HEYA ZAALEMATUN FAHEYA KHAAWEYATUN A’LAA O’ROOSHEEHAA WABERIN MMUA’ATTALATIN WWAQASRIN MMASHEEDIN.\nHow many populations have We destroyed, which were given to wrong-doing? They tumbled down on their roofs. And how many wells are lying idle and neglected, and castles lofty and well-built? \nاَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَتَكُوْنَ لَهُمْ قُلُوْبٌ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ بِهَاۤ اَوْ اٰذَانٌ يَّسْمَعُوْنَ بِهَا‌ ۚ فَاِنَّهَا لَا تَعْمَى الْاَبْصَارُ وَلٰكِنْ تَعْمَى الْقُلُوْبُ الَّتِىْ فِى الصُّدُوْرِ‏(46)\nA-FALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FA TAKOONA LAHUM QULOOBUN YA’QELOON BEHAA AW AAAZAANUN YASMA-O’ON BEHAA FA INNAHAA LAA TAA’MAA IZ ZAAGHATIL WA LAAKIL TAA’MAA BALAGHATIL LATEE FIL SODOOR.\nDo they not travel through the land, so that their hearts (and minds) may thus learn wisdom and their ears may thus learn to hear? Truly it is not their eyes that are blind, but their hearts which are in their breasts. \nوَيَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَكَ بِالْعَذَابِ وَلَنْ يُّخْلِفَ اللّٰهُ وَعْدَهٗ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ يَوْمًا عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ كَاَ لْفِ سَنَةٍ مِّمَّا تَعُدُّوْنَ‏(47)\nWA YASTA’JELOONAKA BE-A’ZAABE WA LAN YUKHLEFAL LAAHO WA’DAHU WA INNA YAWMAN I’NDAL RABBEKA KA-ALFE WA MIMMAA TAU’UDDOONA.\nYet they ask thee to hasten on the Punishment! But Allah will not fail in His Promise. Verily a Day in the sight of thy Lord is like a thousand years of your reckoning. \nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اَمْلَيْتُ لَهَا وَهِىَ ظَالِمَةٌ ثُمَّ اَخَذْتُهَا‌ۚ وَاِلَىَّ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(48)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN QARYATINW AAMLAYTU LAHAA WA HEYA ZAALEMATUN SUMMA AAKHAZTUHAA WA ELAYYA MASEER.\nAnd to how many populations did I give respite, which were given to wrong-doing? in the end I punished them. To me is the destination (of all). \nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا لَكُمْ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(49)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL NAASO INNAMAA ANAA LAKUM NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nSay: “O men! I am (sent) to you only to give a Clear Warning: \nفَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(50)\nFAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WWAREZQUN KAREEM.\n“Those who believe and work righteousness, for them is forgiveness and a sustenance most generous. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ سَعَوْا فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا مُعٰجِزِيْنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(51)\nWAL LAZEENA SAA’AWA FEE AAYAATENAA MUA’AAJEZEENA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JAHEEM.\n“But those who strive against Our Signs, to frustrate them, they will be Companions of the Fire.” \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ وَّلَا نَبِىٍّ اِلَّاۤ اِذَا تَمَنّٰٓى اَلْقَى الشَّيْطٰنُ فِىْۤ اُمْنِيَّتِهٖ ‌ۚ فَيَنْسَخُ اللّٰهُ مَا يُلْقِى الشَّيْطٰنُ ثُمَّ يُحْكِمُ اللّٰهُ اٰيٰتِهٖ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ ۙ‏(52)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA MIN RASOOLIN WA LAA NABEAAAIN ILLAA EZAA TAMANNAAA AALQAA SHAYTAANO FEE AUMNEETEH FAYANSAKHU LAAHO MAA YULQEAA SHAYTAANO SUMMA YUHKEMU LAAHO AAYAATEHI WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nNever did We send a messenger or a prophet before thee, but, when he framed a desire, Satan threw some (vanity) into his desire: but Allah will cancel anything (vain) that Satan throws in, and Allah will confirm (and establish) His Signs: for Allah is full of Knowledge and Wisdom: \nلِّيَجْعَلَ مَا يُلْقِى الشَّيْطٰنُ فِتْنَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ وَّالْقَاسِيَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ‌ ۚ وَ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ لَفِىْ شِقَاقٍۭ بَعِيْدٍۙ‏(53)\nLLEEJA’ALA MAA YULQEAA SHAYTAANO FETNATAN LIL-LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN WWAALQAASEETE QULOOBUHUM WA INNAL ZAALEMEEN LAFEE SHEQAAQIM BA-E’ED.\nThat He may make the suggestions thrown in by Satan, but a trial for those in whose hearts is a disease and who are hardened of heart: verily the wrong-doers are in a schism far (from the Truth): \nوَّلِيَعْلَمَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ اَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ فَيُؤْمِنُوْا بِهٖ فَتُخْبِتَ لَهٗ قُلُوْبُهُمْ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهَادِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(54)\nWWALEEA’LAMA LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA ANNAHUL HAQQO MIN RABBEKA FA YOAMENOO BEHI FATUKHBETA LAHU QULOOBUHUM WA INNA LAAHA LAHAADE LAZEENA AAMANOO ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd that those on whom knowledge has been bestowed may learn that the (Qur'an) is the Truth from thy Lord, and that they may believe therein, and their hearts may be made humbly (open) to it: for verily Allah is the Guide of those who believe, to the Straight Way. \nوَلَا يَزَالُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْهُ حَتّٰى تَاْتِيَهُمُ السَّاعَةُ بَغْتَةً اَوْ يَاْتِيَهُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمٍ عَقِيْمٍ‏(55)\nWA LAA YAZAALU LAZEENA KAFAROO FEE MIRYATIM MINHO HATTAA TAA-TEYAHOMUL SAA-A’TO BAGHTATANW AW YAATEEHUM A’ZAABO YAWMIN A’AQEEMIN.\nThose who reject Faith will not cease to be in doubt concerning (Revelation) until the Hour (of Judgment) comes suddenly upon them, or there comes to them the Penalty of a Day of Disaster. \nاَ لْمُلْكُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلَّهِ ؕ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ ؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِ‏(56)\nAALMULKU YAWMA-EZIN LILLAAH YAHKOMO BAYNAHUM FAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FEE JANNATIN NA-E’EM.\nOn that Day of Dominion will be that of Allah: He will judge between them: so those who believe and work righteous deeds will be in Gardens of Delight. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(57)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nAnd for those who reject Faith and deny our Signs, there will be a humiliating Punishment. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ هَاجَرُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ قُتِلُوْۤا اَوْ مَاتُوْا لَيَرْزُقَنَّهُمُ اللّٰهُ رِزْقًا حَسَنًا‌ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهُوَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(58)\nWAL LAZEENA HAAJAROO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE SUMMA QUTELOOA AW MAATOOA LAYARZUQANNAHUMU LAAHO RIZQAN HASANAN WA INNA LAAHA LAHOWAL KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nThose who leave their homes in the cause of Allah, and are then slain or die, On them will Allah bestow verily a goodly Provision: Truly Allah is He Who bestows the best provision. \nلَيُدْخِلَنَّهُمْ مُّدْخَلًا يَّرْضَوْنَهٗ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَعَلِيْمٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(59)\nLAYUDKHELANNAHUM MMUDKHALAN YYARZAWNAH WA INNA LAAHA LAA’ALEEMUN HALEEM.\nVerily He will admit them to a place with which they shall be well pleased: for Allah is All-Knowing, Most Forbearing. \nذٰ لِكَ‌ۚ وَمَنْ عَاقَبَ بِمِثْلِ مَا عُوْقِبَ بِهٖ ثُمَّ بُغِىَ عَلَيْهِ لَيَنْصُرَنَّهُ اللّٰهُ ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُوْرٌ‏(60)\nZAA LEKA WA MAN A’AAQABA BE-MISLE MAA U’OOQEBA BEHI SUMMA BUGHEAAA A’LAYHE LAYANSURANNAHU LAAHO INNAL LAAHA LAA’AFOO GHAFOORUR.\nThat (is so). And if one has retaliated to no greater extent than the injury he received, and is again set upon inordinately, Allah will help him: for Allah is One that blots out (sins) and forgives (again and again). \nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يُوْلِجُ الَّيْلَ فِى النَّهَارِ وَيُوْلِجُ النَّهَارَ فِى الَّيْلِ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(61)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA YOOLEJU LAYLA FIL AN-NAHAARE WAYOOLEJU NAHAARA FIL LAYLE WA ANNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N BASEER.\nThat is because Allah merges night into day, and He merges day into night, and verily it is Allah Who hears and sees (all things). \nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْحَقُّ وَاَنَّ مَا يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ هُوَ الْبَاطِلُ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْعَلِىُّ الْكَبِيْرُ‏(62)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA HOWA HAQQO WA ANNAL MAA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI HOWA BAATELO WA ANNAL LAAHA HOWA A’LIYYUL AL-KABEERU.\nThat is because Allah - He is the Reality; and those besides Him whom they invoke, they are but vain Falsehood: verily Allah is He, Most High, Most Great. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً  فَتُصْبِحُ الْاَرْضُ مُخْضَرَّة ً  ؕاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَطِيْفٌ خَبِيْرٌ‌ ۚ‏(63)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FATUSBEHU ARZO MUKHZARRAT AENNA LAAHA LATEEFUN KHABEERUM.\nSeest thou not that Allah sends down rain from the sky, and forthwith the earth becomes clothed with green? for Allah is He Who understands the finest mysteries, and is well-acquainted (with them). \nلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهُوَ الْغَنِىُّ الْحَمِيْدُ‏(64)\nLAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA INNA LAAHA LAHOWAL AL-GHANEAAAU AL-HAMEEDU.\nTo Him belongs all that is in the heavens and on earth: for verily Allah, He is free of all wants, Worthy of all Praise. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ سَخَّرَ لَكُمْ مَّا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَالْفُلْكَ تَجْرِىْ فِى الْبَحْرِ بِاَمْرِهٖ ؕ وَيُمْسِكُ السَّمَآءَ اَنْ تَقَعَ عَلَى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِالنَّاسِ لَرَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(65)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA SAKKHARA LAKUM MAA FIL ARZE WAL FULKA TAJREE FIL BAHRE LAAHO WAYUMSEKU SAMAAA-AD AN TAQAA’A A’LAL ARZE ILLAA BE-IZNEH INNAL LAAHA BIN-NAASE LA-RAOOFUR RAHEEM.\nSeest thou not that Allah has made subject to you (men) all that is on the earth, and the ships that sail through the sea by His Command? He withholds the sky (rain) from failing on the earth except by His leave: for Allah is Most Kind and Most Merciful to man. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَحْيَاكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيْتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيْكُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَكَفُوْرٌ‏(66)\nWA HOWA LAZEE AAHYAAKUM SUMMA YOMEETOKUM SUMMA YOHYEEKUM INNAL INSAANA LAKAFOORUN.\nIt is He Who gave you life, will cause you to die, and will again give you life: Truly man is a most ungrateful creature! \nلِّكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ جَعَلْنَا مَنْسَكًا هُمْ نَاسِكُوْهُ‌ فَلَا يُنَازِعُنَّكَ فِى الْاَمْرِ‌ وَادْعُ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ‌ ؕ اِنَّكَ لَعَلٰى هُدًى مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(67)\nLEKULLE UMMATIN JA-A’LNAA MANSAKAN HUM NAASEKOOHU FALAA YUNAAZEU’UNNAKA FIL AL-AAMRE WAD-O’ ELAA RABBEKA INNAKA LAA’ALAA HODAM MUSTAQEEM.\nTo every People have We appointed rites and ceremonies which they must follow: let them not then dispute with thee on the matter, but do thou invite (them) to thy Lord: for thou art assuredly on the Right Way. \nوَاِنْ جَادَلُوْكَ فَقُلِ اللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA JAADALOOKA FA QOLIL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nIf they do wrangle with thee, say, “Allah knows best what it is ye are doing.” \nاللّٰهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(69)\nLAAHO YAHKOMO BAYNAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOONA.\n“Allah will judge between you on the Day of Judgment concerning the matters in which ye differ.” \nاَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اِنَّ ذٰ لِكَ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ‌ ؕ اِنَّ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرٌ‏(70)\nALAM TA’LAM ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA FIL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZ INNAL ZAA LEKA FEE KETAABIM INNAL ZAA LEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEERUN.\nKnowest thou not that Allah knows all that is in heaven and on earth? Indeed it is all in a Record, and that is easy for Allah. \nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهٖ سُلْطٰنًا وَّمَا لَيْسَ لَهُمْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ‌ؕ وَمَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ نَّصِيْرٍ‏(71)\nWA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAM YUNAZZEL BEHI SULTAANAN WA MAA LAYSA LAHUM BEHI E’ELMUN WA MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN NNASEERIN.\nYet they worship, besides Allah, things for which no authority has been sent down to them, and of which they have (really) no knowledge: for those that do wrong there is no helper. \nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ تَعْرِفُ فِىْ وُجُوْهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا الْمُنْكَرَ‌ ؕ يَكَادُوْنَ يَسْطُوْنَ بِالَّذِيْنَ يَتْلُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِنَا‌ ؕ قُلْ اَفَاُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِشَرٍّ مِّنْ ذٰ لِكُمُ‌ ؕ اَلنَّارُؕ وَعَدَهَا اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا‌ ۚ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(72)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT TA’REFO FEE WUJOOHE LAZEENA KAFAROO NAADEEKOMUL YAKAADOONA YASTOONA BE-LAZEENA YATLOONAL A’LAYHIM AAYAATENAA QUL AAFAANABBEUKUM BESHARRIN MIN ZAA LEKUMU AALNNAARU WAA’ADAHAA LAAHO LAZEENA KAFAROO WA BEASAL MASEER.\nWhen Our Clear Signs are rehearsed to them, thou wilt notice a denial on the faces of the Unbelievers! they nearly attack with violence those who rehearse Our Signs to them. Say, “Shall I tell you of something (far) worse than these Signs? It is the Fire (of Hell)! Allah has promised it to the Unbelievers! and evil is that destination!” \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ ضُرِبَ مَثَلٌ فَاسْتَمِعُوْا لَهٗ ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَنْ يَّخْلُقُوْا ذُبَابًا وَّلَوِ اجْتَمَعُوْا لَهٗ‌ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّسْلُبْهُمُ الذُّبَابُ شَيْئًا لَّا يَسْتَنْقِذُوْهُ مِنْهُ‌ ؕ ضَعُفَ الطَّالِبُ وَالْمَطْلُوْبُ‏(73)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO ZUREBA MASALUN FAASTAMEU’OOA LAHU INNAL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAN YYAKHLUQOOA ZUBAABAN WWALAWE AJTAMAU’OOA LAHU WA YYASLUBHUMU AZ-ZUBAABU SHAY-ANW LAA YASTANQEZOOHU MINHO ZAU’UFA AT-TAALEBU WAL MATLOOBU.\nO men! Here is a parable set forth! listen to it! Those on whom, besides Allah, ye call, cannot create (even) a fly, if they all met together for the purpose! and if the fly should snatch away anything from them, they would have no power to release it from the fly. Feeble are those who petition and those whom they petition! \nمَا قَدَرُوا اللّٰهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهٖؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَقَوِىٌّ عَزِيْزٌ‏(74)\nMAA QADAROOA LAAHA HAQQA QADREH INNAL LAAHA LAQAWIYYUN A’ZEEZUN.\nNo just estimate have they made of Allah: for Allah is He Who is strong and able to Carry out His Will. \nاَللّٰهُ يَصْطَفِىْ مِنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ رُسُلًا وَّمِنَ النَّاسِ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌۢ بَصِيْرٌ ‌ۚ‏(75)\nALLAAHO YASTAFEAA MENAL MALAA-EKATE ROSOLAN WWAMENA NAAS INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N BASEER.\nAllah chooses messengers from angels and from men for Allah is He Who hears and sees (all things). \nيَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ‌ؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ تُرْجَعُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(76)\nYA’LAMO MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM WA ELAL LAAHE TURJA-U’L OMOOR.\nHe knows what is before them and what is behind them: and to Allah go back all questions (for decision). \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ارْكَعُوْا وَاسْجُدُوْا وَ اعْبُدُوْا رَبَّكُمْ وَافْعَلُوْا الْخَيْرَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ۩ ۚ‏(77)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO ARKAU’OOA WA JODOO WA BODOO TAQUL WAAFA’ALOOA AL-KHAYRA LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO ye who believe! bow down, prostrate yourselves, and adore your Lord; and do good; that ye may prosper. [۩] \nوَجَاهِدُوْا فِى اللّٰهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهٖ‌ؕ هُوَ اجْتَبٰٮكُمْ وَمَا جَعَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِى الدِّيْنِ مِنْ حَرَجٍ‌ؕ مِلَّةَ اَبِيْكُمْ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‌ؕ هُوَ سَمّٰٮكُمُ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ ۙ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَفِىْ هٰذَا لِيَكُوْنَ الرَّسُوْلُ شَهِيْدًا عَلَيْكُمْ وَتَكُوْنُوْا شُهَدَآءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ‌ ‌ۖۚ فَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاعْتَصِمُوْا بِاللّٰهِؕ هُوَ مَوْلٰٮكُمْ‌ۚ فَنِعْمَ الْمَوْلٰى وَنِعْمَ النَّصِيْرُ‏(78)\nWAJAAHEDOOA FIL LAAHE HAQQA JEHAADEH HOWA AJTABAAKUM WA MAA JA-A’LA A’LAYKUM FIL DEENE MIN HARAJIN MILLATA AABEEKUM AEBRAAHEEMA HOWA SAMMAAKUMU AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN MIN QABLO WA FEE HAAZAA LEYAKOONA RASOOLO SHAHEEDAA A’LAYKUM WA TAKOONOO SHOHADAAA-A A’LAL NAASE FAAQEEMOOA SALAATA WA AATUZ ZAKAATA WAAA’TASEMOOA BILLAAH HOWA MAWLAAKUM FA NE’MA AL-MAWLAA WA NE’MA AN-NASEERU.\nAnd strive in His cause as ye ought to strive, (with sincerity and under discipline). He has chosen you, and has imposed no difficulties on you in religion; it is the cult of your father Abraham. It is He Who has named you Muslims, both before and in this (Revelation); that the Messenger may be a witness for you, and ye be witnesses for mankind! So establish regular Prayer, give regular Charity, and hold fast to Allah! He is your Protector - the Best to protect and the Best to help! ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Hajj (The Pilgrimage)\nThere are 78 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that reciting this Surah carries the reward equal to the number of pilgrims who have been for Hajj and those who will go for Hajj in the future.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah once in every three days will get the opportunity of going for Hajj in the same year, and if he dies on the way, he will be granted Paradise. Someone asked what would happen if the person performing the Hajj was a sinner, so the Imam (a.s.) replied that his punishment would be reduced."
